[{:db/id "q-126610/selection/bce0ae63c1eb1f2f68593236573a59a7c40c29ba31c5820f2e097065cbcc9a44" :answer/id #uuid "6a1934bf-2016-5008-b0cc-a0077ed316e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126610/selection/91a56c9ebd88540750c4d41ce57f76c068208aaf66ad08083bd748ab4c68e2fb" :answer/id #uuid "8a44d7f3-bbd7-5a4a-a5c5-8c675db4d021" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126610/selection/cc4cc66e8683778caad7f6d9f651aa39b54e5a57780a51e6cc97052b03fc196c" :answer/id #uuid "b0508f1b-bb41-503f-9caa-b4b5857f0b51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126610/selection/73260b893a8f48ad043531ae0ead0dc5673ffe2e769042138118122799af3c2a" :answer/id #uuid "cfe25412-aca3-52ce-bb04-b89c67e7ed75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126610/selection/c0fda7833bc32762b9bf81f4457b06b166a1f5f62af5c8c5fff02416fa21a0e5" :answer/id #uuid "7b91a85b-e310-5180-a96c-d697f2407821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126610/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7737d57c-a033-549d-8c34-3c3ece78ebcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126610/selection/91a56c9ebd88540750c4d41ce57f76c068208aaf66ad08083bd748ab4c68e2fb" :answer-field/choices ["q-126610/selection/bce0ae63c1eb1f2f68593236573a59a7c40c29ba31c5820f2e097065cbcc9a44" "q-126610/selection/91a56c9ebd88540750c4d41ce57f76c068208aaf66ad08083bd748ab4c68e2fb" "q-126610/selection/cc4cc66e8683778caad7f6d9f651aa39b54e5a57780a51e6cc97052b03fc196c" "q-126610/selection/73260b893a8f48ad043531ae0ead0dc5673ffe2e769042138118122799af3c2a" "q-126610/selection/c0fda7833bc32762b9bf81f4457b06b166a1f5f62af5c8c5fff02416fa21a0e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126610" :question/id #uuid "e2f2469e-26cc-5373-b28c-d53223eec629" :question/math-academy-id "q-126610" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082799/assets/aa927160974aa22e09f1a8c0b47d588a63f22fc2dd018c3bba36d4a00c649435.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ that lies between $y=0$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. What integral gives the area of the surface generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from $y=0$ to $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\sqrt{1+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126610/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bff48a7c-66d6-55e8-99a1-ae8c80925335"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126610"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126615/selection/57991a1fd0638115a980f43e782ba4da87f9148d816d86ecfa5e9f37c739a0f4" :answer/id #uuid "d0316645-8395-54ae-864d-8433236e7125" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1-y+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126615/selection/7d7783393815da7ca76e36cf681f08363eb09199250796842016bf7b9cab8c9f" :answer/id #uuid "0a83360b-0d84-5897-b17c-d907e07c09b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\sqrt{2-2y+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126615/selection/4c2c1123bf06ccfe54276f40d521123984eecd9aadfb6d466b8d30b3b3e7b413" :answer/id #uuid "dafdbaf9-8aee-5b0b-a710-bd03f9c6d673" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126615/selection/32539c0e154992c35eb6c887c4391c260d1103d6f57ce7b48196139a2fa6eaed" :answer/id #uuid "3bec4232-6c73-5939-a1e8-8ac3d0dfab87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}{(1-y)}^{2}\\sqrt{2-2y+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126615/selection/43c606f3ad3309c2a9572f73e62785f4e8914b019b2edcd4f0c5bfb3f3510ea8" :answer/id #uuid "df071846-265f-5e7b-969f-4008b36ee11a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1-2y+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126615/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b89eac6-b9ab-5277-b118-d44214515dd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126615/selection/7d7783393815da7ca76e36cf681f08363eb09199250796842016bf7b9cab8c9f" :answer-field/choices ["q-126615/selection/57991a1fd0638115a980f43e782ba4da87f9148d816d86ecfa5e9f37c739a0f4" "q-126615/selection/7d7783393815da7ca76e36cf681f08363eb09199250796842016bf7b9cab8c9f" "q-126615/selection/4c2c1123bf06ccfe54276f40d521123984eecd9aadfb6d466b8d30b3b3e7b413" "q-126615/selection/32539c0e154992c35eb6c887c4391c260d1103d6f57ce7b48196139a2fa6eaed" "q-126615/selection/43c606f3ad3309c2a9572f73e62785f4e8914b019b2edcd4f0c5bfb3f3510ea8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126615" :question/id #uuid "e80b22b7-d962-5938-af93-f2a5f86bbdff" :question/math-academy-id "q-126615" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082799/assets/ae26451a8f2962ed873fc5eb703197375bc1a02eff2240bd21cebac81ef26205.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $x=y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}$ that lies to the right of the $y$-axis between its $y$-intercepts. What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2y-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ y(2-y) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $y=0$ to $y=2.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})=1-y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1+{(1-y)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1+(1-2y+{y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})\\sqrt{2-2y+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126615/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bff48a7c-66d6-55e8-99a1-ae8c80925335"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126615"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109237/selection/baf01c5df9a2b7b98b99b1862a249c9d20212a9da38a3fa1e5707c7cfd38ff16" :answer/id #uuid "6108cb78-bb5e-58f6-8fe1-1f29295c8b39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109237/selection/86126cacabfc67dda65cc0682762353eda92c845733cf4d51a955259c3ba20ce" :answer/id #uuid "ce4230f9-0ed1-5e41-a369-2fef50a5b75c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109237/selection/d6c9eb28975368ee775928724837c47788e0f06b8354e08809227a0baa6b8fc9" :answer/id #uuid "3e93f3d1-a196-5cfb-85f9-7ee88ab1d8d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109237/selection/372bdc81a4309cc258d785cac17c3be37454a3424c6f978d7a1275740da9a305" :answer/id #uuid "00520f55-4bf3-5694-ba03-a5d373d8d96d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109237/selection/1d051b71a951dde68e06b804d0a8eb3f780b3a1703909dd813c473f912e102c6" :answer/id #uuid "c861f554-d898-5e76-90fa-330abe831192" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109237/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23a0b2b7-29a1-5e2c-88af-78b72cd8fee8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109237/selection/baf01c5df9a2b7b98b99b1862a249c9d20212a9da38a3fa1e5707c7cfd38ff16" :answer-field/choices ["q-109237/selection/baf01c5df9a2b7b98b99b1862a249c9d20212a9da38a3fa1e5707c7cfd38ff16" "q-109237/selection/86126cacabfc67dda65cc0682762353eda92c845733cf4d51a955259c3ba20ce" "q-109237/selection/d6c9eb28975368ee775928724837c47788e0f06b8354e08809227a0baa6b8fc9" "q-109237/selection/372bdc81a4309cc258d785cac17c3be37454a3424c6f978d7a1275740da9a305" "q-109237/selection/1d051b71a951dde68e06b804d0a8eb3f780b3a1703909dd813c473f912e102c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109237" :question/id #uuid "58c515e6-dbc9-5e2a-acb7-4ae381a18c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-109237" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082799/assets/2baa8f39370b831bd8306aa3eb60e5d16d54ce50474f873f0fa329c069d61689.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ that lies between $y=1$ and $y=e,$ as shown above. What integral gives the area of the surface generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from $y=1$ to $y=e.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{1}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{{y}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109237/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bff48a7c-66d6-55e8-99a1-ae8c80925335"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109237"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-109253"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082799/assets/12d30907e2fb6cdd031134a667c7de1324fec66025c0f2029b18f4521e94da83.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $x=3+2y-{y}^{2}$ that lies to the right of the $y$-axis between its $y$-intercepts. What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+2y-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-2y-3 & =0 \\\\ (y+1)(y-3) & =0 \\\\ y & =-1,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $y=-1$ to $y=3.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3+2y-{y}^{2})=2-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{3}(3+2y-{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1+{(2-2y)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{3}(3+2y-{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}-8y+4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{3}(3+2y-{y}^{2})\\sqrt{4{y}^{2}-8y+5}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-109258/selection/8348769b3b51d0929872be86e3c6ada4518344040bd17e9de3de557fc368dfcb" :answer/id #uuid "9ecaec5a-0d7f-5b85-84fe-2f9e982bf2b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}(-{y}^{2}+8y-12)\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+6}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109258/selection/8f77913cc09c3a0b06e2ca2d193cefc660f64a069175258cdf0f92723c8d2d48" :answer/id #uuid "0ea68a15-7001-5b69-ab88-6bf65be04dc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+6}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109258/selection/05970955ba2d26c0e68104d423c7f2bd71d40dd5cc486ff9a76fa9543ec0ca63" :answer/id #uuid "b3881748-5c50-584d-acd2-28a17c0ad4d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{6}(y-4)\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-2y+5}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109258/selection/f5e9ff4aec1f32fc053400ccde16402203df942bc43fbc100f306b547207e243" :answer/id #uuid "b1d9ce2a-8f22-5c9f-854e-89dd07bc91a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{6}(y-4)\\sqrt{4{y}^{2}-32y+65}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109258/selection/ba7aba09fde14b3f1ae20e53edc5927b099935ce2e8cfc204c56227f1e02719a" :answer/id #uuid "6532a921-7fea-5e87-973c-0531a31714d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{6}(-{y}^{2}+8y-12)\\sqrt{4{y}^{2}-32y+65}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109258/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "356b928a-f168-5aae-bf5c-de994cab5562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109258/selection/ba7aba09fde14b3f1ae20e53edc5927b099935ce2e8cfc204c56227f1e02719a" :answer-field/choices ["q-109258/selection/8348769b3b51d0929872be86e3c6ada4518344040bd17e9de3de557fc368dfcb" "q-109258/selection/8f77913cc09c3a0b06e2ca2d193cefc660f64a069175258cdf0f92723c8d2d48" "q-109258/selection/05970955ba2d26c0e68104d423c7f2bd71d40dd5cc486ff9a76fa9543ec0ca63" "q-109258/selection/f5e9ff4aec1f32fc053400ccde16402203df942bc43fbc100f306b547207e243" "q-109258/selection/ba7aba09fde14b3f1ae20e53edc5927b099935ce2e8cfc204c56227f1e02719a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109258" :question/id #uuid "e3a98f8f-e2c5-5fe4-a763-31a2ca07130e" :question/math-academy-id "q-109258" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082799/assets/3d01ddb2278875780397e90a9d6f6ad6b2fc44890c59faab7a69b8ebcb5d210b.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $x=4-(y-4)^{2}$ that lies in the first quadrant between its $y$-intercepts. What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-(y-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =2,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $y=2$ to $y=6.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(4-(y-4)^{2})=8-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{6}(4-(y-4)^{2})\\sqrt{1+{(8-2y)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{6}(-{y}^{2}+8y-12)\\sqrt{4{y}^{2}-32y+65}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109258/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bff48a7c-66d6-55e8-99a1-ae8c80925335"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109258"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126715/selection/c24b8f5f7cd8d67dfdb5f5890b3da833cb70ff66c527099da3046c0d655d2863" :answer/id #uuid "6744aee8-7138-5a4a-bd63-338733a357ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-16x+17}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126715/selection/cc99fa6901402cf8c53efde1845338493c65d9251fe610354fec6b2f69f8aec6" :answer/id #uuid "c486d335-9233-5c80-9e60-39fae11f7f7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{3}({x}^{2}-4x+3)\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-16x+17}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126715/selection/868c411ebf26414a2d42a715000a83c9694e9a8b543400a6b14cd1a2e2fb5fb1" :answer/id #uuid "5d5f09cd-5729-5c47-a05a-11c75c7807fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-16x+17}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126715/selection/af85ba0aa5e2dca14e0e19a4c962e66bbbe7d1b866a2cdd9c2f22441ac269898" :answer/id #uuid "334b6284-3f1f-5823-a2d1-4eac5dadc478" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}({x}^{2}-4x+3)\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-16x+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126715/selection/d2df15f72abf04ee78d861edb64783a16368ad670f6d3c6503a8824dbc4a2001" :answer/id #uuid "4b6e1fdc-2408-53c8-aee4-5ccbcbfb3f11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-16x+1}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126715/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d497aea2-9b5f-57c4-8de0-b75d780c782d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126715/selection/868c411ebf26414a2d42a715000a83c9694e9a8b543400a6b14cd1a2e2fb5fb1" :answer-field/choices ["q-126715/selection/c24b8f5f7cd8d67dfdb5f5890b3da833cb70ff66c527099da3046c0d655d2863" "q-126715/selection/cc99fa6901402cf8c53efde1845338493c65d9251fe610354fec6b2f69f8aec6" "q-126715/selection/868c411ebf26414a2d42a715000a83c9694e9a8b543400a6b14cd1a2e2fb5fb1" "q-126715/selection/af85ba0aa5e2dca14e0e19a4c962e66bbbe7d1b866a2cdd9c2f22441ac269898" "q-126715/selection/d2df15f72abf04ee78d861edb64783a16368ad670f6d3c6503a8824dbc4a2001"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126715" :question/id #uuid "fcb08d10-5de4-50f1-acf0-54b821666e7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-126715" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14082799/assets/bbdb10a20dd90cd0928e91851662fccaf8d0b03e86c44f58b5311ba805183e8e.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $y={x}^{2}-4x+3$ that lies in the fourth quadrant between its $x$-intercepts. What integral gives the area of the surface generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi x\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+3 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x-3) & =0 \\\\ x & =1,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=1$ to $x=3.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-4x+3)=2x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}x\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\sqrt{1+{(2x-4)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-16x+17}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126715/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7cf4318c-a323-5224-92df-879ebc2bf3b0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109418/selection/3b8f2642c3908cb3f857b7793604094c7e458be78f8f1aaa53287ce882d6e37d" :answer/id #uuid "b23462b9-6e6a-5b7b-b2ae-2dc8b1d4cd82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-4x+5}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109418/selection